"Continue the visual overhaul (second round) of the Waldorf community task manager (Hungarian UI) on branch feature/visual-overhaul-navigation. Fix: (1) Every list item should be one whole-card clickable element, including the admin lists (e.g. \"Feladatcsere-kérelem\" in Jóváhagyások, Nyilvántartások, Feladatok és események, Archívum and other admin lists) and the teacher schedule and anywhere else such items appear: remove the separate \"Részletek\" link and make the whole item the link, for every role, not only the group admin. (2) Fix translation: English state words such as \"pending\", \"approved\", \"active\", \"archived\" shown in lists must be Hungarian everywhere. (3) Notifications (parent \"Értesítések\"): the whole notification card is one clickable element (opens it) and \"Olvasottnak jelölöm\" becomes a separate checkbox on the right side of the card. (4) Notifications text alignment: the card content is currently hugging the left edge; add proper padding and alignment. (5) When a profile is opened, the welcome message heading has a blue focus rectangle around it: remove it (do not break accessibility; the focus move must stay programmatic without a visible ring on non-interactive headings). (6) Give the top menu items proper button styling (pill or tab buttons with hover, pressed and current-page state) instead of plain underlined links. (7) Open a default page for every profile instead of the welcome page: Szülő goes to Értesítések; Óvónő goes to Beosztás and the teacher gets no menu bar at all because that is their only page; both admin profiles (group admin and super admin) go to Áttekintés. (8) The menu items are confusing: the group admin initially sees 3 menu items (Áttekintés, Feladatok, Jóváhagyások) but after clicking any of them sees 5 (Áttekintés, Nyilvántartások, Feladatok és események, Jóváhagyások, Archívum); the super admin has a similar mismatch (8 on the welcome page versus 9 afterwards, with different names such as Feladatok vs Feladatok és események and Nyilvántartások in a different position). Make the menu identical and consistent on every page of a profile (same items, same labels, same order), including the new default page. Keep the existing design (terracotta palette, logo, cards). Apply the same UI/UX best practices as before: accessibility (one accessible name per whole-card control, focus-visible states, 44 px targets), responsive layout, tests updated and extended, user guide updated. Screenshots from the user show the current state of the admin approvals list, admin records list, parent notifications, welcome heading, and the super admin and group admin menus."
